  "frontier_coordinate": "R-131 fixes the exact finite-cylinder response factorization only after an owner-complete physical form is supplied and isolates a floor-uniform deterministic current-square H2 component. It proves that diagonal sample Grams omit the mixed replica response and that bounded multipliers alone cannot yield dyadic mixed/far decay. The exact conditional acceptance simplex is available once the production constants are supplied. The Xi radial coefficient Gram is quantitatively positive on active strata but does not control the full tangent norm after only the common-phase quotient and degenerates at the pure-singlet transition; every fixed finite-doublet-second-moment heat law also loses uniform transversality along large singlet rays. The live successor is A13-CLASSII-MIXED-REPLICA-SEXTIC-TRANSVERSAL-RESPONSE-BOUND: construct the owner-complete mixed replica form, derive production-specific spatial shell estimates and global c_bal, and couple the Xi radial and wedge channels to an owner-compatible sextic, source, heat, or low transverse complement. Then compute D, K, R0, S0, matching energy, the absolute anchor, and apply the R-129 shifted-Douglas criterion once. R-130, R-129, R-128, R-127, R-125, R-123, R-120, R-119, R-103 REG, and R-087/R-093 CORE retain their owners. OVERLAP_src, Nelson, removals, interacting measure, and Sector A remain open.",
